1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:03,822
This is Niramoy, a voice-first medical pre-screening

2
00:00:03,822 --> 00:00:06,663
system I built for clinics in Bangladesh.

3
00:00:06,863 --> 00:00:10,155
The patient starts here. No app and no account.

4
00:00:10,155 --> 00:00:12,816
Just a mobile number, typed, or spoken

5
00:00:12,816 --> 00:00:15,268
digit by digit into the microphone.

6
00:00:15,468 --> 00:00:18,640
A one-time code signs them in. It is hashed,

7
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,740
single-use, and it expires in five minutes.

8
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:25,539
Now the core of the system. The assistant asks its

9
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:28,563
question aloud and on screen, and then the

10
00:00:28,563 --> 00:00:31,658
microphone opens by itself. Nothing to tap.

11
00:00:31,658 --> 00:00:34,249
The portal says so in its own words.

12
00:00:34,449 --> 00:00:37,949
The whole portal runs in Bangla or English, and the

13
00:00:37,949 --> 00:00:41,242
patient can answer in Bangla, in Banglish, or in

14
00:00:41,242 --> 00:00:43,644
their own regional way of speaking.

15
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:47,316
For this recording I am using the typing fallback,

16
00:00:47,316 --> 00:00:51,204
because this capture environment has no live microphone.

17
00:00:51,204 --> 00:00:55,023
The same flow accepts voice in the running application.

18
00:00:55,223 --> 00:00:59,013
Everything else is live. The assistant works through its

19
00:00:59,013 --> 00:01:02,059
questions, and every answer goes into exactly

20
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:04,631
the same pipeline the microphone uses.

21
00:01:04,831 --> 00:01:08,307
And whatever the patient gives, it is stored exactly

22
00:01:08,307 --> 00:01:11,315
as they said it. Never edited, never cleaned.

23
00:01:11,315 --> 00:01:14,857
That is the first rule this whole system is built on.

24
00:01:15,057 --> 00:01:18,478
And at the end of the visit, the patient leaves with

25
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:21,965
their own copy. The whole conversation, exactly as it

26
00:01:21,965 --> 00:01:26,044
was captured, generated automatically and handed back to them.

27
00:01:26,244 --> 00:01:29,767
When a patient submits, the case moves to the medic's

28
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:32,824
queue, ordered by urgency rather than arrival.

29
00:01:32,824 --> 00:01:36,015
This one is Critical, and it carries a red flag.

30
00:01:36,215 --> 00:01:39,991
Here is that patient's own conversation. The follow-up

31
00:01:39,991 --> 00:01:43,488
questions the system asked, in Bangla and English,

32
00:01:43,488 --> 00:01:47,124
and the answers, word for word. Underneath, the AI's

33
00:01:47,124 --> 00:01:50,201
structured reading of the same conversation,

34
00:01:50,201 --> 00:01:51,809
in ten clinical fields.

35
00:01:52,009 --> 00:01:55,119
The medic checks the machine's reading against the

36
00:01:55,119 --> 00:01:57,856
patient's own words, records the vitals, and

37
00:01:57,856 --> 00:02:00,095
forwards the case to a named doctor.

38
00:02:00,295 --> 00:02:04,099
The doctor's case opens with safety. A rule-based check

39
00:02:04,099 --> 00:02:07,350
found chest pain in the patient's own words and

40
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:10,601
forced the tier to Critical. That rule is local

41
00:02:10,601 --> 00:02:13,852
and deterministic. The model can raise concern.

42
00:02:13,852 --> 00:02:15,996
It can never suppress the rule.

43
00:02:16,196 --> 00:02:19,739
Beside it sits the stored explainable-AI reason.

44
00:02:19,739 --> 00:02:23,282
Then the doctor writes the diagnosis themselves.

45
00:02:23,282 --> 00:02:25,939
The AI's suggestion never enters it.

46
00:02:25,939 --> 00:02:29,039
The system narrows. The clinician decides.

47
00:02:29,239 --> 00:02:32,683
Accepting the case writes the encounter as an

48
00:02:32,683 --> 00:02:36,280
HL7 FHIR R4 document bundle, with the patient's

49
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:40,336
verbatim words carried through, and the risk exported

50
00:02:40,336 --> 00:02:43,703
as a RiskAssessment rather than a diagnosis.

51
00:02:43,703 --> 00:02:47,607
The same record renders as a PDF a person can read.

52
00:02:47,807 --> 00:02:50,526
The patient speaks. The system structures.

53
00:02:50,526 --> 00:02:53,052
The medic verifies. The doctor decides.

54
00:02:53,052 --> 00:02:55,124
And it becomes a medical record.

